## THE COMMISSION
One small, behaviour-neutral CI hygiene change the product owner's board already holds as a ticket: give three workflows an explicit read-only token so CodeQL alerts #1-#3 can close on the merge, without touching what any job does. The product owner's standing rule (merge-once-tested; a gate before every merge; CodeQL is organisational policy, C-190, never bypassed, never dismissed) applies: you build and measure, a tier-1 gate re-measures (a workflow change gets its own review: RD-814 says so), Tuesday opens the PR, reads the runs and CodeQL, and lands.

