**Step 3, the check program, RED FIRST (written and run BEFORE any edit; no jest, no network).** Write `session-tools/b632/perm_check.rb` (Ruby `yaml`, stdlib only; `python3 -I` has no yaml module and `actionlint` is not installed: say both in STATUS with the `which` output). For every file in `.github/workflows/*.yml` it must: (a) parse with `YAML.load_file` (print `PARSE OK` or the error); (b) read the workflow-level `permissions` and, per job, the job-level one; (c) compute each job's EFFECTIVE permissions = the job's own mapping if present, else the workflow's, else `nil`; (d) print one line per job: file, job id, effective permissions as sorted `key=value` pairs; (e) print `LEAST-PRIVILEGE` for a job only when the effective mapping is exactly `{"contents" => "read"}`, else `NOT-LEAST (<reason>)` (`nil`, `write-all`, `read-all`, any `write`, any extra key). **Run at the clone's HEAD (= main, before any edit): expected `build.yml`/`build`, `deploy.yml`/`build` and `npm-audit.yml`/`audit` read `NOT-LEAST (nil)` (RED, the three alerts' state); `gitleaks.yml` and `arm-ttk.yml` (job-level `contents: read`) read `LEAST-PRIVILEGE`; `deploy-demo.yml` reads `NOT-LEAST` for both of its jobs (workflow-level `id-token: write` + `contents: read`) and is the in-run control that the program does fire on a non-least mapping. All six parse OK.** Save the output. A different pattern at main (for example one of the three already has a block) is a finding: STOP and say so.

**Step 4, the edit (one insertion per file, by program, then read back).** Write `session-tools/b632/apply.rb` (or any small script; the editor tool is also fine) that, for each of the three files, asserts the line `jobs:` occurs exactly once, then inserts these four lines immediately BEFORE it (ASCII, LF endings, no trailing spaces, the file's existing line endings preserved; check `file` shows no CRLF at main first):
```
# RD-814: least privilege for GITHUB_TOKEN; this workflow only reads the repository.
permissions:
  contents: read

```
(The fourth line is the blank line; the result reads: previous blank line, the comment, `permissions:`, `  contents: read`, a blank line, `jobs:`.) The same four lines in all three files. Nothing else changes: no re-indent, no re-wrap, no touched comment. **A hand edit that changes anything else is a STOP; if the editor adds a trailing newline or changes an ending, the numstat in Step 5 will show it.**

**Step 5, the measurements (by program, each with a control that can fail).**
